# This repository is the harness's reference instance, so it takes the seed's own line-ending
# rules (harness/templates/seed/.gitattributes) and extends them over the sources it ships.
#
# Git for Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` in its SYSTEM config at install time; without this
# file a Windows clone gets a CRLF worktree, and the rungs that compare or parse bytes rather
# than lines read that as damage — the secret scan flagged every text file in the tree, and the
# integrity rung reported five present scripts as deleted (DC-030).
* text=auto eol=lf
